From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BD-J: list each stream type in PlayItem.getComponents()

PlayItemImpl.getComponents() filled the audio, PG, IG and secondary
video/audio lists from clip.getVideoStreams(). A BD-J Xlet asking a play
item for its components got the video streams six times over, labelled
as video, audio, subtitles, data, secondary video and secondary audio,
and never the real audio or subtitle streams. Use the matching TIClip
getter for each list; they return the arrays the clip was built with
(the stream-count getters already rely on them being non-null).

Unchanged in libbluray 1.5.1 and master.

diff -ruN a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/bluray/ti/PlayItemImpl.java b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/bluray/ti/PlayItemImpl.java
--- a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/bluray/ti/PlayItemImpl.java	2026-09-25 16:55:22.061404335 -0400
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/bluray/ti/PlayItemImpl.java	2026-09-25 16:55:22.099464775 -0400
@@ -67,11 +67,11 @@
 
     public ServiceComponent[] getComponents() {
         StreamInfo[] video = clip.getVideoStreams();
-        StreamInfo[] audio = clip.getVideoStreams();
-        StreamInfo[] pg = clip.getVideoStreams();
-        StreamInfo[] ig = clip.getVideoStreams();
-        StreamInfo[] secVideo = clip.getVideoStreams();
-        StreamInfo[] secAudio = clip.getVideoStreams();
+        StreamInfo[] audio = clip.getAudioStreams();
+        StreamInfo[] pg = clip.getPgStreams();
+        StreamInfo[] ig = clip.getIgStreams();
+        StreamInfo[] secVideo = clip.getSecVideoStreams();
+        StreamInfo[] secAudio = clip.getSecAudioStreams();
 
         int count = video.length + audio.length + pg.length + ig.length + secVideo.length + secAudio.length;
 
